00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Laughter]  [Music]  [Laughter]  hi  members of the yale graduating class of  2021 i'm robert lopez je class  of 1997. i'm a songwriter  best known along with my wife kristen  for co-writing the song  let it go and all the songs from frozen  frozen two  and most recently the theme songs for  one division  and i am so excited to get to be this  year's yale class day speaker  my time at yale was one of the  highlights of my life there hasn't been  a day that i haven't thought about some  great person i knew  great book i read a great memory i have  from yale  after i graduated i moved back home with  my parents without whose fierce support  i could never have  had a career in the arts i joined a  musical theater songwriting workshop  where i met jeff marks  with whom i wrote the show avenue q and  kristen anderson who became my wife  and my work wife my lyricist and my love  and somewhere along the way i co-wrote  the book of mormon with matt stone and  trey parker  over the span of my career i've been  able to share in many awards but always  in collaboration with some wonderful  person  so on class day i plan to talk about the  saving grace  of collaboration and friendship and how  it can take the weight of the world off  your stressed out shoulders  and i'll reflect a little on my time at  yale and share a memory and probably  even a song or two of course my speech  will only be part of the great tradition  of class day  i've spoken to the class day committee  and i'm so impressed with them and  everything they're planning it's going  to be great  so i want to say thanks to president  salove and everyone at yale for  entrusting me with this  it's a huge honor and i'm really looking  forward to seeing you on class day on  may 23rd thank you

